    <h1 class="hero-title">The Two Infinities<br><em>(and Beyond)</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">The Geometry of Existence, from Zero and One to Consciousness, Gravity, and the Cosmic Ledger
      &middot; {{ site.author }}</p>
    <p class="lede">&ldquo;The universe exists not because something caused it &mdash; but because nothing is
      geometrically impossible.&rdquo;</p>
    <div class="claims">
      <p class="claims-kicker">The framework in twelve claims</p>
      <ol class="claims-list">
        <li><strong>Existence needs no cause.</strong> It needs only that nothing forbid it &mdash; and
          geometry forbids nothing here. <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--chosen">position</span></li>
        <li><strong>There are two infinities and they are not the same size.</strong> Downward into the
          interval, uncountable; upward through counting, countable. Cantor proved the inequality.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--known">theorem</span></li>
        <li><strong>That inequality is the tilt.</strong> More room on one side than the other, which is
          where the framework says the direction of time comes from.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--weak">weakest joint</span></li>
        <li><strong>π is the condition of a universe, not a constant inside one.</strong> Zero and one
          cannot be joined by a straight path; joining requires curving, and curving is π.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--chosen">position</span></li>
        <li><strong>The universe is an integration, not a thing being integrated.</strong> A sum being
          taken &mdash; quantity is the residue the gathering leaves behind.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--chosen">position</span></li>
        <li><strong>The sum never converges.</strong> Eternal is arithmetic, not sentiment: linear deposit
          makes each stage last 1/n, and Σ1/n diverges.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--known">theorem</span></li>
        <li><strong>Nothing damps it.</strong> There is no outside for the energy to leave to, so the
          swing never settles &mdash; exact in its law, incomputable in its future.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--chosen">position</span></li>
        <li><strong>dx is a completed act, not a vanishing quantity.</strong> The smallest gathering
          actually carried through; its grain is set by thermodynamics, not by choice.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--chosen">position</span></li>
        <li><strong>A self is an operation, not a thing.</strong> A life is the integral of its moments,
          and it has no last term to arrive at.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--chosen">position</span></li>
        <li><strong>What sits below one still accumulates.</strong> As temperature is nothing one molecule
          has, deposits under the threshold become a measurable gradient &mdash; and at density, a new
          state rather than more of the same. <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--weak">no derivation yet</span></li>
        <li><strong>Return without repetition requires a torus; a change of side without a crossing
          requires a half-twist.</strong> Four shapes are available and the framework claims no more than
          that. <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--known">topology</span></li>
        <li><strong>Polarity is residue, and galaxies should carry its handedness.</strong> The ledger's
          running total &mdash; and the one place the whole structure can be killed by a survey.
          <span class="claim-tag claim-tag--test">testable</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="claims-foot">Four of these are standard results the framework borrows and claims no credit
        for. Six are positions it holds and argues. Two are debts. One is a prediction with its failure
        conditions written down in advance. <a href="/foundations/#t-eternal-integration">The thesis in
        full</a> &middot; <a href="/stress-tests/">where it is attacked</a>.</p>
    </div>

