    <h2 id="t-the-chain-of-necessity">The Chain of Necessity</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Six links, each one forced by the one before it. If the chain holds, existence is
      not a gift that was granted but a shape that could not be avoided.</p>
  </div>

  <aside class="fundamental" aria-labelledby="t-fundamental-one">
    <p class="fundamental-tag">Fundamental&nbsp;I</p>
    <div class="fundamental-head">
      <h3 id="t-fundamental-one">Read this first. Nothing later works without it.</h3>
      <p>This is the first of the fundamentals, and it is the one the whole framework is balanced on.
        Every chapter that follows &mdash; the torus, the seam, the ledger, the splice &mdash; assumes
        the reader has this chain in hand. <strong>Understanding it is not optional.</strong> If the six
        links below do not yet feel forced, go no further until they do: read it twice, and read it
        slowly.</p>
    </div>

