    <p class="plate-note">Halving π does not produce a smaller, tamer quantity. e<sup>iπ/2</sup> = i: it
      creates an axis perpendicular to the real line that was simply not there before. Quantum information
      experiments have since shown that a quantum theory stripped of its imaginary axis makes worse
      predictions than our universe obeys &mdash; the imaginary dimension is load-bearing, not decorative.
      <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
  </figure>

    <p class="fundamental-foot">Hold on to one sentence: <strong>zero and one cannot be joined by a
      straight line, so the path must curve, and the constant of all curving is π.</strong> Everything
      else on this site is that sentence, carried further.</p>

    <p class="fundamental-thesis">And the whole of it in one sentence, for anyone who wants the
      position before the argument: <strong>the universe is an eternal integration of opposing
      infinities, which together swing like an out-of-control pendulum.</strong>
      <a href="/foundations/#t-eternal-integration">Every word of that is technical, and it is unpacked
      here</a> &mdash; the two infinities are of different cardinalities, the integration is improper and
      divergent, and the pendulum is the one real system whose critical orbit has an infinite period.</p>

    <div class="fundamental-list">
      <p class="kicker">The six fundamentals</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>I &mdash; The chain.</strong> Zero and one cannot be joined straight, so the path
          curves, and π is the condition of there being anything at all. <em>This plate.</em></li>
        <li><a href="/the-self/#t-fundamental-two"><strong>II &mdash; A self is an operation.</strong></a>
          An integral, not a substance: a running sum taken over moments too small to be felt
          singly.</li>
        <li><a href="/skeletal-splice/#t-fundamental-three"><strong>III &mdash; Accumulation is the
          mechanism.</strong></a> One infinitesimal self is beneath measurement; enough of them are
          not &mdash; and the sum is a different kind of thing from its terms.</li>
        <li><a href="/torus/#t-fundamental-four"><strong>IV &mdash; Return without repetition.</strong></a>
          The torus is the smallest shape that can both come back and keep count.</li>
        <li><a href="/moebius/#t-fundamental-five"><strong>V &mdash; The half-twist.</strong></a>
          Inversion without a boundary being crossed; i is that strip caught mid-turn.</li>
        <li><a href="/cosmic-ledger/#t-fundamental-six"><strong>VI &mdash; A structured zero.</strong></a>
          Three poles, three degrees of completion, and a dark sector that needs no new particle.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted xsmall">Six plates across the site carry this border. Everything else is
        argument, evidence or vision built on top of them.</p>
    </div>
