<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Five Joins</p>
    <h2 id="t-four-joins">Where the Framework Touches Something Testable</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Most of what follows is geometry argued carefully. Four places are different:
      they are the points where the geometry reaches out and takes hold of a measured thing, and could be
      caught doing it wrongly. If you read nothing else, read these.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3><a href="/moebius/#t-colour">The seam and the colour charge</a></h3>
      <p>The strong force is the one place nature already insists that a charge can never be exhibited
        alone &mdash; only ever as a colour bound to its own inversion. That is not a metaphor for a
        one-sided surface. It is the definition of one. Z&#8322; for the twist, Z&#8323; for the colour, and
        an honest account of why the multiplication is a resemblance rather than a derivation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3><a href="/moebius/#t-handedness">Why galaxies have a rotation bias</a></h3>
      <p>158 clockwise against 105 counterclockwise in JWST's deep field, and a dipole that reverses across
        a plane. A single twist predicts the wrong thing. A twist that births an inverted <em>pair</em>
        predicts a sign flip &mdash; and one clean, perfectly odd great circle, which the sky can
        refuse.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3><a href="/cosmic-ledger/#t-dark-matter">Dark matter as the ledger's middle entry</a></h3>
      <p>26.95 per cent sits at the π/2 pole: integrated far enough to curve space, not far enough to carry
        a phase and therefore not far enough to shine. Dark because of where it stopped, not because of what
        it is made of &mdash; and the flat rotation curve falls out of the gradient.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3><a href="/cosmic-ledger/#t-proton-electron">One thing at two phases</a></h3>
      <p>Proton and electron carry charges equal to one part in 10<sup>21</sup> &mdash; an equality with
        no explanation unless they are related by a symmetry. The framework reads them as the same
        geometry at two degrees of completion: one closed, one turned over.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3><a href="/spiral/#t-quarks">The thirty-six, the quarks, and the pace</a></h3>
      <p>666 is T<sub>36</sub>, and thirty-six is exactly the quark census: six flavours, three colours,
        two signs. More importantly the triangular increment is n, which makes the tick 1/n, which makes
        the harmonic series diverge &mdash; the skeleton that sets the pace is the reason the One is
        unreachable.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
