<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">The Standing Rule of This Site</p>
    <h2 id="t-earned-chosen-refused">Earned, Chosen, Refused</h2>
    <p>Every chapter of the Unified Edition closes with a section headed <em>What Is Earned and What Is
      Chosen</em>, and every page here keeps that habit. <strong>Earned</strong> means it follows by
      argument or arithmetic and can be checked. <strong>Chosen</strong> means it is an interpretation laid
      over the mathematics &mdash; coherent, but not forced. <strong>Refused</strong> means it was available,
      it would have been dramatic, and it was left out because it is costume rather than structure.</p>
    <p class="muted">The framework is stronger for saying which is which. A reader who cannot tell the
      theorem from the vision has not been given the work; they have been given a mood.</p>
  </div>
</section>
